From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
Subject: mips: DMA: post-DMA cache flush on 1004K/34K without IOCU

EcoNet EN7528 (dual-core 1004Kc, 4 VPEs) and EN751221 (34Kc, 2 VPEs)
have CONFIG_CPU_HAS_PREFETCH but no IOCU, so device DMA does not snoop
the L1/L2 caches. Linux only performs arch_sync_dma_for_cpu() when
cpu_needs_post_dma_flush() is true; 1004K/34K are not in that list and
do not implement MAAR, so dma_sync_single_for_cpu() is a no-op.

On SMP a foreign core can speculatively fill a DMA buffer (page_pool
recycle, skb head, etc.) while the engine is still writing. The stale
line later writebacks over a kmem_cache object — seen as:

  CPU n Unable to handle kernel paging request
  kmem_cache_alloc_noprof / inet_twsk_alloc
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

after a Wi-Fi client joins and generates TCP TIME_WAIT churn. maxcpus=1
hides it by removing the other L1; it is not a driver regression.

Treat 1004K and 34K like BMIPS5000: invalidate after DMA_FROM_DEVICE,
and write back the L2 lines at the buffer edges on 1004K (it has an
inclusive scache; 34Kc typically does not).

Signed-off-by: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
--- a/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
@@ -31,8 +31,16 @@ static inline bool cpu_needs_post_dma_flush(void)
 	case CPU_R10000:
 	case CPU_R12000:
 	case CPU_BMIPS5000:
 	case CPU_LOONGSON2EF:
 	case CPU_XBURST:
+	/*
+	 * 1004Kc (EN7528) and 34Kc (EN751221) implement prefetch but
+	 * EcoNet parts have no IOCU, so DMA is not hardware-coherent.
+	 * Post-DMA invalidate is required on SMP or recycled buffers
+	 * write back into the slab allocator.
+	 */
+	case CPU_1004K:
+	case CPU_34K:
 		return true;
 	default:
 		/*
 		 * Presence of MAARs suggests that the CPU supports
